THE ERROR, named precisely. I found C4 carries many senses, and my reflex was Q209: WHICH SENSE
GOVERNS WHEN TWO DISAGREE. That is the `seams` tiebreaker rule, and I applied it to the wrong
kind of thing. The seams canon is about EVIDENCE -- two representations of ONE truth that can
silently split, where you must name the tiebreaker before the risky operation. A name carrying
several senses is the opposite shape: ONE representation of SEVERAL truths, none of them
competing to be the same fact. Carrying the tiebreaker rule across is `fantasy-operational-
boundary` exactly -- the mechanism transferred and its moral load inverted. Closing that seam
would have destroyed the generative property and protected nothing.
